From: The-going <48602507+The-going@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 4 Sep 2026 14:22:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] drm/sun4i: tcon: set the pad select bit

The TCON global control register carries a pad select bit that routes the
TCON's output to the external pads.  Without it the pipeline configures
and the connector reports connected, but no signal reaches the HDMI
transmitter.

Set it unconditionally in tcon bind.

Taken from the Armbian sunxi-6.12 tree
(patch: add-TCON-global-control-reg-for-pad-selection.patch), rebased
onto mainline.  Carried here so the H616 HDMI series is reproducible.


---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_tcon.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_tcon.c
index bf405a2aa..42d58b6fd 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_tcon.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_tcon.c
@@ -1248,6 +1248,10 @@ static int sun4i_tcon_bind(struct device *dev, struct device *master,
 		goto err_free_dclk;
 	}
 
+	regmap_update_bits(tcon->regs, SUN4I_TCON_GCTL_REG,
+			   SUN4I_TCON_GCTL_PAD_SEL,
+			   SUN4I_TCON_GCTL_PAD_SEL);
+
 	if (tcon->quirks->has_channel_0) {
 		/*
 		 * If we have an LVDS panel connected to the TCON, we should
